From 169fae09602b46d4bb902f3bd8647381ab1a42eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:36:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/35] Safarium: About page shows the updater's status and the
 Safarium version
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The About page (chrome://settings/help) still said "Automatic updates are
unavailable in this build": Safarium builds compiled out its update
status because Chromium's own updater is off. Safarium now has its own,
so the page listens again and VersionUpdater::Create returns a Safarium
updater backed by the shared release check (safarium_update_check.h,
also the base of the menu's Check for Updates…):
- checking, then "Safarium is up to date" with the check mark;
- "Safarium fix<N> is available. Choose Safarium › Check for Updates…
  to install it." when GitHub has a newer release;
- "Safarium couldn't check for updates…" when the feed can't be read;
- nothing for unstamped development builds.
The version line now starts with the Safarium version: "Safarium fix5 ·
Chromium Version …" or "Local build <commit>, based on fix5 · …".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
